#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:1
msgid "1. Hello World"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:3
msgid ""
"Launching a tile kernel starts `N` concurrent copies of the same function. "
"Each copy is a *tile program* (also called a *tile block*): a single logical "
"thread operating on a multi-dimensional tile of data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:7
msgid ""
"**Note**: Tile programs run concurrently, but the CUDA runtime may not run "
"all of them at the same time. Communication between tile programs requires "
"detailed knowledge of the CUDA runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:11
msgid ""
"![Thread-centric vs Tile-centric GPU programming models](../_static/images/"
"mental-model-shift.svg)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:11
msgid "Thread-centric vs Tile-centric GPU programming models"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:15
msgid "Here is a kernel that prints \"hello\" from the GPU:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:17
msgid ""
"use cutile::error::Error;\n"
"use cutile::prelude::*;\n"
"\n"
"#[cutile::module]\n"
"mod hello_world_module {\n"
"    use cutile::core::*;\n"
"\n"
"    #[cutile::entry()]\n"
"    fn hello_world_kernel() {\n"
"        let pid0 = program_id(0);\n"
"        let pid1 = program_id(1);\n"
"        let pid2 = program_id(2);\n"
"        let n0 = num_programs(0);\n"
"        let n1 = num_programs(1);\n"
"        let n2 = num_programs(2);\n"
"        cuda_tile_print!(\n"
"            \"Hello from program <{}, {}, {}> in a grid of <{}, {}, {}> "
"programs!\\n\",\n"
"            pid0, pid1, pid2,\n"
"            n0, n1, n2\n"
"        );\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"use hello_world_module::hello_world_kernel;\n"
"\n"
"fn main() -> Result<(), Error> {\n"
"    let device = Device::new(0)?;\n"
"    let stream = device.new_stream()?;\n"
"    let launcher = hello_world_kernel();\n"
"    launcher.grid((2, 2, 1)).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"    Ok(())\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:52
msgid "**Output:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:54
msgid ""
"Hello from program <0, 0, 0> in a grid of <2, 2, 1> programs!\n"
"Hello from program <1, 0, 0> in a grid of <2, 2, 1> programs!\n"
"Hello from program <0, 1, 0> in a grid of <2, 2, 1> programs!\n"
"Hello from program <1, 1, 0> in a grid of <2, 2, 1> programs!\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:61
msgid ""
"Four tile programs were executed by the CUDA runtime, each printing its own "
"coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:66
msgid "GPU vs. CPU Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:68
msgid ""
"`cutile-rs` programs have two parts: code that runs on the GPU, or the "
"*device-side*, and code that runs on the CPU, or the *host-side*. The "
"following snippet will JIT-compile to the GPU when executed from the host-"
"side:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:71
msgid ""
"#[cutile::module]\n"
"mod hello_world_module {\n"
"    use cutile::core::*;\n"
"\n"
"    #[cutile::entry()]\n"
"    fn hello_world_kernel() {\n"
"        // This code runs on the GPU!\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:83
msgid "`#[cutile::module]` marks a module as containing GPU code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:84
msgid "`#[cutile::entry()]` marks a function as a kernel entry point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:86
msgid ""
"Each coordinate in the launch grid gets one instance of the kernel function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:89
msgid "The following host-side code will launch the device-side code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:91
msgid ""
"fn main() -> Result<(), Error> {\n"
"    let device = Device::new(0)?;             // Connect to GPU\n"
"    let stream = device.new_stream()?;             // Create a work queue\n"
"    let launcher = hello_world_kernel();   // Get the kernel launcher\n"
"    launcher.grid((2, 2, 1)).sync_on(&stream)?; // Launch 2×2×1 = 4 "
"programs\n"
"    Ok(())\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:101
msgid ""
"Host-side code sets up the GPU, specifies the kernel launch grid, and "
"launches the kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:105
msgid "Program IDs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:107
msgid ""
"Each tile program is assigned an ID along each axis of the 3-dimensional "
"launch grid, following Triton's `tl.program_id(axis)` / `tl."
"num_programs(axis)`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:109
msgid ""
"let pid0 = program_id(0);   // This program's index along grid axis 0\n"
"let n0 = num_programs(0);   // The grid extent along axis 0\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:114
msgid ""
"For each axis `k`, `0 <= program_id(k) < num_programs(k)`. The tuple forms "
"`get_tile_block_id()` and `get_num_tile_blocks()` return all three "
"coordinates at once."
msgstr ""

