#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:122
msgid "Under the hood"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:124
msgid ""
"**At compile time:** `#[cutile::module]` captures your Rust code as an AST."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:125
msgid ""
"**At first kernel launch:** The AST is compiled to Tile IR bytecode → cubin "
"(GPU binary)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/01-hello-world.md:126
msgid ""
"**Cached:** The compiled kernel is cached in memory for the rest of the "
"process, so later launches of the same variant skip compilation. Caching "
"across processes (an on-disk cubin cache) is opt-in; see [Compilation](../"
"guide/jit-compilation.md)."
msgstr ""

